Insertion sort in Pascal, an example of the logic (check the syntax of your own compiler):

```pascal
type List = array[0..100] of integer;

procedure InsertionSort(var a: List; n: integer);
var i, j, key: integer;
begin
  for i := 2 to n do
  begin
    key := a[i];
    j := i - 1;
    while (j >= 1) and (a[j] > key) do
    begin
      a[j + 1] := a[j];
      j := j - 1
    end;
    a[j + 1] := key
  end
end;
```
Pascal does not guarantee that the second part of `and` is skipped when the first is false, so the array starts at index 0 to make the read of `a[0]` harmless.
